casebook flow-current-consistency v1
source "quorum fixture: implies" dated 2026-10-09 by "quorum project"
note "A pump cannot move water without drawing motor current. If the flow switch says it is, either the flow switch"
note "is lying or the current channel is dead -- and a dead channel reads exactly like a quiet one."

observe flow_high     "discharge flow above minimum"
observe current_high  "motor current above no-load"
observe level_low     "sump level low"
observe priming       "operator is priming the pump"

implies flow_high current_high "moving water draws motor current"

claim dry_run   "pump running dry"                needs current_high level_low
excuse priming_run "operator priming, dry running expected briefly" needs priming
priming_run undercuts dry_run
flow_high rebuts dry_run

action continue idle
action inspect  when mismatch__flow_high__current_high
action shutdown safe when dry_run
prefer shutdown over inspect over continue
